# Booking — Manager Combined Multi-Resource Day Grid (M22-S05, UC-057)
# TenantContext populated from X-Tenant-ID / X-Actor-ID headers (set by BFF).
# MANAGER-only — same restriction tier as Resource Management
# (docs/14-API_CONTRACTS.md § GET /schedule/day-grid).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl = {{backendUrl}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH — combined day grid for a given date
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### Get the day grid
# Each block carries `gap` (M18-S10): the time the resource stays held after the booking and why —
#   { "source": "SERVICE_BUFFER" | "RESOURCE_TURNOVER", "minutes": 60, "serviceName": "Polimento" | null }
# `serviceName` is set only for SERVICE_BUFFER. `gap` is null for a row with no recorded gap
# (no gap, or written before the gap columns existed) and for a CLASS_SESSION.
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedule/day-grid?date=2026-06-01
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

###

### STAFF role → 403 (MANAGER-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedule/day-grid?date=2026-06-01
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF
